    </div>
    <ul class="roundtable-fit-list">
      <li>Licensed or supervised mental health professionals</li>
      <li>Clinicians working in private practice, health systems, community care, education, or training</li>
      <li>People who have encountered AI use in clinical work, whether helpful, concerning, ambiguous, or difficult to classify</li>
      <li>Professionals willing to listen across disciplines and speak without sharing identifying client information</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="roundtable-conversation">
    <div class="section-shell roundtable-conversation-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">The conversation</p>
      <h2>What we will explore together</h2>
      <div class="roundtable-question-grid">
        <p>How is AI showing up in therapeutic relationships now?</p>
        <p>What benefits, risks, and blind spots are clinicians noticing?</p>
        <p>What helps patients disclose AI use without shame?</p>
        <p>Where do existing clinical frameworks help, and where do they leave gaps?</p>
        <p>What language, tools, education, or safeguards would be most useful next?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

